# N4 (LMX_semantics.ru.md #argument-compatibility-stage, #method-parts; Codex OPUS-CODEX-20261015-19): D lacks the
# y the code S declares. The call admission fails when the program runs, before S runs: the implicit call throw,
# taken by catch: call. D\x keeps 10 though the first statement of S writes x. Translation accepts it. Entry 7.
S:
    int: x 1
    int: y 5
end: S
D:
    int: x 10
end: D
fn: run () int
    int: r 82
    call: S D
    catch: call ()
        r: 83
        if: D\x = 10
            r: 7
    ---
return: r
int: got run()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: got; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
